# Cinefield Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Defense in depth: the provider-worker Dockerfile only COPYs the specific
# directories it needs, but this file keeps secrets and unrelated bulk out of
# the build context sent to the daemon in the first place — so a future
# broader COPY (or a different Dockerfile) can't accidentally bake one in.

# Secrets — never send an env file to the Docker daemon. .env.example is
# safe (placeholders only) and explicitly re-included.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Local Supabase CLI state (.temp holds a linked project ref/session, not
# meant for an image).
supabase/.branches
supabase/.temp

# Next.js web app — the provider worker never starts it.
.next
out
public
src/app
src/components
src/hooks
src/context

# Node / build artifacts
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor/OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs and non-runtime project files
docs
*.md
LOCKED_FEATURES.md
CINEFIELD_ARCHITECTURE_CONTRACT_SOURCE.txt

# Test/dev tooling not needed at runtime
playwright-report
test-results
e2e

# Docker meta files themselves
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
